# Deprecated — see `.rules/` and `.cursor/rules/repo-governance.mdc`

This file used to carry the SI-1..SI-10 self-improve iteration rules.
As of v14.2.1 (G-008), the canonical rule sources are
`.rules/workflow.mdc` (SI-1 → W-1, SI-2 → W-2, SI-3 → W-3, SI-4 → W-4,
SI-5 → W-5, SI-6 → W-6, SI-8 → W-7, SI-9 → W-8, SI-10 → W-9),
`.rules/soul.mdc` (SI-7 → S-7), and `.rules/architecture.mdc` (SI-6
token budgets → A-3). This stub remains as a discoverable
cross-reference so existing `.cursor/rules/` auto-load paths still
surface a pointer to the canonical source.

## Canonical rule source

| Layer | Canonical `.mdc` file | Compiled into |
|---|---|---|
| Soul (P0) | `.rules/soul.mdc` | `repo-governance.mdc` + `AGENTS.md` |
| Architecture (P1) | `.rules/architecture.mdc` | `repo-governance.mdc` + `AGENTS.md` |
| Conventions (P2) | `.rules/conventions.mdc` | `repo-governance.mdc` + `AGENTS.md` |
| Workflow (P3) | `.rules/workflow.mdc` | `repo-governance.mdc` + `AGENTS.md` |
| Style (P4) | `.rules/style.mdc` | `repo-governance.mdc` (Cursor only) |

The compiled full corpus lives at `.cursor/rules/repo-governance.mdc` —
that is the file every Cursor agent loads at session start.

## Regenerate after editing `.rules/*.mdc`

```bash
python -c "from devolaflow.local.compiler import RuleCompiler; \
RuleCompiler('.rules/compile-config.yaml').compile_all()"
```

Drift detection (lint enforced by
`tests/test_no_ghost_features.py::test_rule_surfaces_compile_only`):
hand-edits to `.cursor/rules/repo-governance.mdc` or to any deprecated
pointer stub registered in `devolaflow.local.drift::DEPRECATED_STUB_FILES`
(including this file) fail the lint at CI-time.

## Migration

Switch any tooling that reads this file to read either:

* `.cursor/rules/repo-governance.mdc` — compiled full corpus, OR
* the canonical `.rules/*.mdc` layer files listed above.
